WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.923
Step 1. Find the rules. The rules decide which codes the valueset contains.

1.2
00:00:05.923 --> 00:00:09.780
In the Definition section, include rules add codes,

1.3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.306
and exclude rules remove matching codes.

2.1
00:00:13.306 --> 00:00:18.646
Step 2. Choose whether to use the parent rules. If the valueset has a parent,

2.2
00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:24.501
turn on Use parent rules to combine the parent rules with the rules on this page.

3.1
00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:30.907
Step 3. Add a rule. Select Add Rule next to Include rules or Exclude rules.

3.2
00:00:30.907 --> 00:00:34.279
Care adds a rule card and opens it.

4.1
00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:40.914
Step 4. Select the terminology system. In System, select LOINC, SNOMED, or UCUM.

4.2
00:00:40.914 --> 00:00:47.720
An include rule with no concepts and no filters takes every code in its system.

5.1
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.828
Step 5. Add exact codes.

5.2
00:00:49.828 --> 00:00:55.249
Under Concepts, select Add Concept, enter the code, and select Verify.

5.3
00:00:55.249 --> 00:01:01.634
Care fills in the name of the concept. Verify every concept before you save.

6.1
00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.348
Step 6. Add filters.

6.2
00:01:03.348 --> 00:01:08.762
A filter matches a group of codes by a property of the terminology system.

6.3
00:01:08.762 --> 00:01:17.417
Open Advanced: filter by properties, then enter the property, operator and value.

7.1
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:21.190
Step 7. Remove a rule, a concept, or a filter.

7.2
00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:24.483
Select the trash button on a card or a row.

7.3
00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:28.429
If you remove a rule by mistake, select Undo.

8.1
00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:31.611
Step 8. Save the valueset. Select Save.

8.2
00:01:31.611 --> 00:01:35.747
If a rule has an error, its card shows Needs attention,

8.3
00:01:35.747 --> 00:01:41.210
and Care lists the errors under Review these fields before saving.
